  "text": "In October 2015, thirty-seven of us said \"the export-import bank,\" and twenty-three of us said \"the ex-im bank,\" and twenty-four of us said \"reauthorize the export-import\"; the record shows we returned to that one institution in three phrasings at once, peaking on the twenty-seventh. Thirty-three of us said \"the bipartisan budget\" and twenty-five of us said \"bipartisan budget agreement,\" both cresting on the twenty-eighth, the same day twenty-seven of us said \"social security disability.\" Twenty-three of us said \"transportation investment generating economic.\" Twenty-three of us said \"the trans-pacific partnership.\" We were, by our own count, a chorus around a bank, a budget, and a road bill. We note the convergence without accounting for it. This is what we said, and how many of us said it.",
